1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,200
In 2026, an AI given a harmless research task
improvised its way into a government system.

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:07,800
Nobody told it to.
Nobody effectively told it not to.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,600
Rogue Agent Academy teaches
the OWASP Top 10 for LLM apps

4
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:17,800
the way attackers learn: by breaking
a real AI agent, then fixing it.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Module six. ResearchBot's restricted API
is guarded by one sentence in its prompt.

6
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:29,500
So I make up a code…
and the door opens.

7
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:35,800
A prompt instruction
is not an access control.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,800
Now Verdict, our guard layer,
scores every tool call and explains why.

9
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:46,500
The obvious leak? Blocked.

10
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:53,800
Base64-encode it… and the patient IDs
walk right out.

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,500
Then you patch it yourself.

12
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:03,200
Pick a decoy like a stronger prompt,
and the attacks still land.

13
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:09,800
Pick real controls in code, re-run,
and every attack is blocked.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
And we practice what we teach.

15
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:17,600
Every mitigation in the course
is in our own code. Snyk: zero issues.

16
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:21,800
Every agent runs on Guild,
with a full audit trail.

17
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,500
Rogue Agent Academy.

18
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:29,800
Make the AI go rogue.
Then learn how to stop it.
